  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Village Support Group</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Village Support Group (VSG) is a local NGO established since 1995. We have been working for community development for more than 25years at grassroot level in differently project components including: fishery and forestry conservation and improvement, environmental rights development, Good Governance, Advocacy, Rights to access Public information, Agricultural development, Food security, WASH, Nutritional education and Older People Association development.&#x201d; Right to access information&#x201d; is one of the projects that initiated contributions to create the &#x2018;Right to Access Information Law&#x2019; in Cambodia included local administration reform, increased accountability, and transparency. VSG has a good reputation and strong relationship and networking at sub-national level with government agencies, civil societies, private sectors as well as with communities and CBOs.

VSG has target areas in 4 provinces, 20 districts, cities and 22 communes including Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey and Siem Reap provinces.

VSG wants to see:
- natural resources taken care of by the authorities, the community and the Commission on Sustainability,
- fishermen, especially vulnerable people, to have a decent, harmonious life and enough food to have full freedom of expression and decision-making in the community development process,
- community fisheries committees capable of leading, managing, managing work effectively, transparently, accountably and sustainably, and
- local people get comprehensive information, make the right decisions, address challenges and needs from national and sub-national authorities in a transparent and accountable manner.&quot;</narrative>
  </participating-org>
